xtra animate-pulse-glow ring r=28 + stroke-width 3). Zoom In ×2 → label \\\"140%\\\", transform scale(1.4); Zoom Out → \\\"120%\\\", scale(1.2); Reset View → \\\"100%\\\", translate(0,0) scale(1).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-7\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph renders all 19 documents from all 5 modules as nodes plus 19 connection lines matching all related-document pairs. After Reset View (100%, translate 0,0) node bounding box x 390–934, y 20–584 fits entirely within the 1280×643 SVG viewport, i.e. complete graph in view.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-8\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Header nav exposes three buttons: Documents, Knowledge Graph, Favorites (with count). Switched among all three repeatedly; each rendered its own content (document list+detail, graph canvas with controls/legend, favorites list).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-9\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"With doc \\\"Component Library\\\" (Component Structure collapsed, Prop Patterns expanded) and graph zoom 140% + node selected: switching Documents→Graph→Favorites→Documents kept h1=\\\"Component Library\\\", the same per-section expand/collapse states in every tab, and graph zoom 140% / transform scale(1.4) with the node still highlighted. Persisted store shows graphState {zoom:1.4, pan:{0,0}} and per-doc sectionStates. Caveat: drag-panning the canvas never changed pan from (0,0) (both Playwright drag and dispatched mouse sequences), so only the zoom half of view state could be exercised.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"FT-10\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Documents module filter leaks into the Favorites view, hiding favorited documents\", \"actual\": \"Persistence/count/markers work: after page reload favorites were retained (JWT Authentication, Accessibility Standards) with nav badge \\\"Favorites 2\\\"; the badge incremented 1→2 immediately on starring, and markers survived sorting (Title→Last Updated) and module filtering (AUTH). BUT the Favorites view is filtered by the module chosen in Documents: with AUTH selected it listed only JWT Authentication (Accessibility Standards missing); with DATA selected it listed 0 items and showed \\\"No favorites yet - Star documents to add them to your favorites\\\" while the nav badge still read \\\"Favorites 2\\\". The Favorites view has no module filter control of its own, so favorites become unreachable there until the filter is cleared in Documents.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-12\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Visited all 19 documents and collected every content-section reference label and related-document entry; no document listed its own title in either list (selfRefs = []).\"}, {\"item_id\": \"CS-13\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Graph SVG has exactly 19 g.graph-node elements (one per document). Node stroke colors group by module and match the legend swatches (API cyan hsl(187,85%,53%)=rgb(33,213,237), Auth purple, Data Layer green, UI amber, Core red). 19 <line> edges = the 19 unique related-document pairs derived from all documents.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-15\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Section headers carry a chevron-down icon; expanded \\\"REST Principles\\\" has class rotate-180 with visible body paragraph + reference links, while collapsed \\\"Endpoint Naming Conventions\\\"/\\\"Pagination & Filtering\\\" chevrons are un-rotated with no body paragraph. Indicator state matches visibility.\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-16\", \"verdict\": \"FAIL\", \"issue\": \"Graph node selection does not open the document view; a manual tab change is required\", \"actual\": \"Clicking the \\\"Component Library\\\" node on the Knowledge Graph only highlighted the node (pulse-glow ring). The main area still showed only the graph canvas, controls and legend — no document title/sections/related list appeared anywhere, and the active tab stayed on Knowledge Graph. Only after manually clicking the Documents tab did h1 = \\\"Component Library\\\" appear. The graph view (zoom 140%, node selection) was preserved for return.\", \"evidence\": null}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-17\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Clicking \\\"HTTP Methods Guide\\\" link on the collapsed \\\"Endpoint Naming Conventions\\\" section kept h1 = \\\"REST API Design Guidelines\\\" and showed prompt \\\"Please expand the section to access links\\\". After expanding the section, clicking the same link navigated to h1 = \\\"HTTP Methods Guide\\\".\"}, {\"item_id\": \"IX-18\", \"verdict\": \"PASS\", \"issue\": null, \"actual\": null, \"evidence\": \"Search \\\"zzzqqq\\\" → 0 cards with message \\\"No documents found / Try adjusting your search or filter criteria\\\". Search \\\"JWT\\\" + UI module → also 0 cards with the same message. Clearing search restored 3 UI docs; clicking All restored all 19.\"}]}"
